[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 3. She bakes 4 eggs for her friends every day, so that's 4 eggs/day.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 4. The number of eggs that are not eaten or used for baking is \(16 - 3 - 4 = 9\) eggs/day.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 5. She sells these 9 eggs at the farmers' market for $2 per egg.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m So, the total revenue per day is \(9 \text{ eggs} \times \$2/\text{egg} = \$18\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m # Given values
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m total_eggs_per_day = 16
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m eggs_eaten_per_day = 3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m eggs_baked_per_day = 4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m price_per_egg = 2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m # Calculate the number of eggs sold at the farmers' market
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m eggs_sold_per_day = total_eggs_per_day - eggs_eaten_per_day - eggs_baked_per_day
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m # Calculate the total revenue per day
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m total_revenue_per_day = eggs_sold_per_day * price_per_egg
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m print(total_revenue_per_day)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3899417)[0m ```
